content.text:
He reveals the deep and hidden things;
He knows what lies in darkness,
and light dwells with Him.

Doom has come to you,
O inhabitants of the land.
The time has come;
the day is near;
there is panic on the mountains
instead of shouts of joy.

Forge the chain,
for the land is full of crimes of bloodshed,
and the city is full of violence.

He oppresses the poor and needy;
he commits robbery
and does not restore a pledge.
He lifts his eyes to idols;
he commits abominations.

Cry out and wail,
O son of man,
for the sword is wielded against My people;
it is against all the princes of Israel!
They are tossed to the sword with My people;
therefore strike your thigh.

Slash to the right;
set your blade to the left—
wherever your blade is directed.

I will pour out My anger upon you;
I will breathe the fire of My fury against you;
I will hand you over to brutal men,
skilled in destruction.

Now speak a parable to this rebellious house and tell them that this is what the Lord GOD says:
‘Put the pot on the fire;
put it on and pour in the water.

For the blood she shed is still within her;
she poured it out on the bare rock;
she did not pour it on the ground
to cover it with dust.

Pile on the logs and kindle the fire;
cook the meat well
and mix in the spices;
let the bones be burned.

It has frustrated every effort;
its thick rust has not been removed,
even by the fire.

Your heart grew proud of your beauty;
you corrupted your wisdom because of your splendor;
so I cast you to the earth;
I made you a spectacle before kings.

So also Christ did not take upon Himself the glory of becoming a high priest, but He was called by the One who said to Him:
“You are My Son;
today I have become Your Father.”

But My righteous one will live by faith;
and if he shrinks back,
I will take no pleasure in him.”

Tell it to your children;
let your children tell it to their children,
and their children to the next generation.

What the devouring locust has left,
the swarming locust has eaten;
what the swarming locust has left,
the young locust has eaten;
and what the young locust has left,
the destroying locust has eaten.

The seeds lie shriveled beneath the clods;
the storehouses are in ruins;
the granaries are broken down,
for the grain has withered away.

Even the beasts of the field pant for You,
for the streams of water have dried up,
and fire has consumed the open pastures.

Blow the ram’s horn in Zion;
sound the alarm on My holy mountain!
Let all who dwell in the land tremble,
for the Day of the LORD is coming;
indeed, it is near—

They storm the city;
they run along the wall;
they climb into houses,
entering through windows like thieves.

Do not be afraid, O land;
rejoice and be glad,
for the LORD has done great things.

They cast lots for My people;
they bartered a boy for a prostitute
and sold a girl for wine to drink.

Proclaim this among the nations:
“Prepare for war;
rouse the mighty men;
let all the men of war
advance and attack!

Sheol and Abaddon
are never satisfied;
so the eyes of man are never satisfied.

May none who pass by say to them,
“The blessing of the LORD be on you;
we bless you in the name of the LORD.”

O Israel, put your hope in the LORD,
for with the LORD is loving devotion,
and with Him is redemption in abundance.

Surely I have stilled and quieted my soul;
like a weaned child with his mother,
like a weaned child is my soul within me.

Pagkatapos, sabihin mo ang talinghagang ito sa mga rebeldeng mamamayan ng Israel at ipaalam sa kanila: ‘Ito ang sinasabi ng Makapangyarihang Panginoon:
Isalang mo ang kaldero;
lagyan mo ng tubig ang loob nito.

Kaya nagalit ako sa henerasyong ito;
at sinabi ko, ‘Palaging lumalayo ang puso nila sa akin,
at ayaw nilang sumunod sa mga itinuturo ko sa kanila.’

Ang tsismis ay parang pagkaing
masarap nguyain at lunukin;
at nakakarating sa kaloob-looban ng tao.

Buong puso akong lumalapit sa inyo;
kaya akoʼy tulungan ninyo
na huwag lumihis sa mga utos ninyo.

Panginoon, ang salita nʼyo
ay mananatili magpakailanman;
hindi ito magbabago tulad ng kalangitan.

Hirap na hirap na po ako Panginoon;
panatilihin ninyo akong buháy
ayon sa inyong pangako.

Kayo ang kanlungan
at pananggalang ko;
sa inyong mga salitaʼy umaasa ako.

Nanginginig ako sa takot sa inyo;
sa hatol na inyong gagawin
ay natatakot ako.

Tumatawag ako sa inyo;
iligtas ninyo ako, at susundin ko
ang inyong mga tuntunin.

Napakamaawain ninyo Panginoon;
ingatan ninyo ang aking buhay
ayon sa inyong paghatol.
